    <text>
    <body>
        
        <div type="letter">
            <div type="text">
                <opener>
                    <date>May 28/72</date>
                    <salute>Dear Sir</salute>
                </opener>
                <div type="transcription">
                     
<p>If this beginning seems right to you will you kindly send it back to me &amp; I will either finish it before I go or take it with me &amp; send it back by post in the course of a week or two. Neither of these plans will give me any inconvenience so if you would like it done please let me have it again.<ref target="#foot.f1"/></p>
<p>I am dear Sir | Yours truly | Briton Riviere</p> 
                </div>
            </div>

            
            
        </div>

        

        

        <div type="footnotes">
            <note xml:id="foot.f1">Riviere sent a sketch of a friendly dog for inclusion in <ref target="../bibliographies/bibl_2400.xml" resp="#mjhawkins"><hi rend="italic">Expression</hi></ref> (see <ref target="./DCP-LETT-8353.xml" resp="#mjhawkins">letter from Briton Riviere, 26 May 1872</ref>).</note>
        </div>        
            
    </body>
    </text>
